        <node id="n4::n17">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="63.66247011952197" width="184.68706507304114" x="9934.758832763358" y="-352.7188933090729"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="62.8046875" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="182.078125" x="1.3044700365207973" xml:space="preserve" y="0.4288913097609566">There seems to be some debate
over whether the Geats/Gutes
were Gothic, or vice versa, given
their similar locations and names.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n4::n18">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="166.8539707835326" width="198.71309428950872" x="9796.58198036044" y="52.2097548814163"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="165.712890625" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="196.796875" x="0.958109644754586" xml:space="preserve" y="0.5705400792662942">Swedish/Sweden got their names
since the Svear ended up being
the dominant tribe in the region.
Should the name of Sweden be
changed depending on whether
Geats/Gutes end up being dominant
instead, or should a new dynamic
title just be created instead to save
the hassle of editing things in every
game to account for the name
change? (Relevant?)<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n4::n19">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="154.2305444887118" width="211.1361487383797" x="9432.525216041702" y="-559.4540947726664"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="151.01171875" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="212.60546875" x="-0.7346600058099284" xml:space="preserve" y="1.6094128693558787">Base game uses Norse for all of
Scandinavia, then has that split
arbitrarily into Norwegian, Danish,
and Swedish.

Most mods (and it seems historically),
seem to imply Norse would be better
suited just for "proto-Norwegians" (their
tribal identity before unifying into an
actual nation).<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n4::n20">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="111.87995112881808" width="151.8581418326694" x="9249.028897729853" y="-302.18808187169986"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="106.908203125" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="154.0703125" x="-1.1060853336657601" xml:space="preserve" y="2.4858740019090533">The Danic tribes ended up
becoming dominant in their
region, conquering Jutland
from the remaining Jutes,
eventually assimilating them
into a national "Danish"
identity.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
