        <node id="n4::n330">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="49.07419645122499" width="90.58656252642913" x="9098.218981564112" y="181.748090165525"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="48.103515625" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="68.67578125" x="10.955390638215249" xml:space="preserve" y="0.4853404131125103">From
CELTIC
CULTURES<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n4::n331">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="239.09366955056083" width="541.0402342196644" x="9199.109162145389" y="-906.3642228259143"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="239.21875" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="531.888671875" x="4.575781172332427" xml:space="preserve" y="-0.06254022471955523">derekmark's culture mod goes a bit more indepth in the evolution of Germanic cultures compared to
some other mods. It includes a custom culture for Irminonic and Ingvaeonic, proto-Norse, many
pre-Anglo-Saxon cultures, and even a proto-Germanic culture. We could use this to make the
games more historical and dynamic, we just need to determine how indepth we want to go. Should
proto-Germanic ever be used? The mod generalizes the Germanic split by having East Germanic
(Gothic and Vandal) split off in 150 AD, and the rest (proto-Norse, Irminonic, Ingvaeonic, and 
Frankish/Istvaeonic) split off in 200 AD. If we do, we might need to look into limiting proto-Germanic
diverging/hybridizing before they officially split to properly keep the actual Germanic language split
valid.

If we decide to use some of the cultures like proto-Germanic, Ingvaeonic, and Irminonic, then we
will probably need to set something up to ensure the cultures are properly setup depending on the
game's start date. (i.e. None of these three ancestor cultures should appear on start if they set the
game's start date around the base game's start date). This will probably require modifying the
converter to allow using start dates as conditions in culture mappings, or use a lot of game_start
on_action effects to make everything get set properly.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n4::n332">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="223.70991807299447" width="226.87339956116057" x="5704.204820302439" y="-247.70650207835473"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="224.517578125" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="232.123046875" x="-2.6248236569199435" xml:space="preserve" y="-0.4038300260027654">derekmark's culture mod includes
custom Indo-Germanic and
Deccano-Germanic cultures, representing
Germans that migrated to India. It has both
be divergences from proto-Germanic in
100 AD. Realistically, this would likely end
up being an entirely different branch of
Germanic if it diverges like that, so it could
be worth looking into having that be 
represented in the other games as well.

Should they also be modified to actually
reference being a hybrid of Indian cultures,
or should they simply be left as divergent
cultures?<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n4::n333">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="95.46995754371952" width="425.1626907757909" x="8502.911998424217" y="-415.30673883133545"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="92.20703125" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="420.279296875" x="2.441696950394544" xml:space="preserve" y="1.631463146859744">derekmark's culture mod includes an Ingvaeonic culture, which can probably
be used to represent the point in time when these cultures were very similar,
speaking similar languages, then these divergent cultures could be created
representing their unique languages/identities developing. The mod puts these
cultures as forming about 550 AD, after the Anglo-Saxon invasion, so those
could probably just be created right away if they are in the relevant regions.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n4::n334">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="79.95072060518334" width="233.79778992318597" x="9198.727426118516" y="-522.3141828309022"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="77.505859375" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="234.384765625" x="-0.29348785090769525" xml:space="preserve" y="1.222430615091639">derekmark's culture mod has a proto-Norse
culture to represent when North Germanic
diverged from proto-Germanic. Can maybe
use that and have it split into the regional
cultures like Dane, Norse, Svear, etc.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
