    <node id="n5">
      <data key="d6">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry height="403.2871880584327" width="336.43484429895443" x="4222.292890176804" y="-1378.3117693809397"/>
          <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
          <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="400.931640625" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="336.712890625" x="-0.13902316302301188" xml:space="preserve" y="1.177773716716274">SOME NOTES ON CREATION NAMES:

- Creation names will always have a key/ID associated with
them. From there, the default localization keys for that
creation name are &lt;key&gt;_name, &lt;key&gt;_collective_noun,
and &lt;key&gt;_prefix.

- The key/ID for a creation name CAN be the same as the
ID for a predefined culture. For example, you can create a
creation name that has 'french' as it's key, despite a culture
already existing with that as it's ID.

- The &lt;key&gt;_name localization key for a creation name
CAN NOT be localized the same as an existing culture. For
example, if you create a creation name with the key
'french_2', but localize it's name as french_2_name: "French",
then this creation name WILL NEVER WORK!

- Special characters can be used to make a name localization
be considered different. The best thing to use is [U+200B],
the Zero-Width Space, which will make the name localization
look EXACTLY the same as a predefined one, but it's
considered different. For example, this is the base game
localization for the 'english' culture: "English". But, this is the
localization for a working creation name that looks similar, but
is considered different: "English​". At the end of the localization,
there is a Zero-Width Space, which makes it different.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
