shown here are the "fallback"
mappings, so the ones used
outside of special circumstances.

In the converter right now, ALL
Latin/Italic cultures (with the
exception of Venetic/Histrian)
convert to Roman if under a
Roman tag. (Will need to add
the Venetic cultures as well
when updating all the mappings).

When converting to EU4/5, the
non-Roman cultures should
have their own non-Latinized
versions. Historically, since Rome
more or less assimilated these
cultures, it is hard to say any
potential cultures that should
be mapped from them that aren't
considered Roman-/Latinized,
so the main culture evolutions
actually being shown will likely
just be the Romance ones.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
