              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="106.908203125" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="658.3046875" x="3.15504431199588" xml:space="preserve" y="0.19229843750008513">For the Romance cultures, I will be listing two possible ways the culture could be created. One will list the regions Roman
could be in in Imperator so the culture will exist at game start if in the regions. The other will be what sort of cultures Roman
could hybridize with in CK3 to make it appear.

For these hybrid cultures, I think they should be made to have their original Heritage, but speak Latin (or a custom relevant
dialect Language), to represent how these cultures mainly consist of the peoples from that region being Romanized, not
Romans themselves moving into the region in droves. (i.e. Gallo-Roman would have Gaulish Heritage, but speak Latin).<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
