        <node id="n6::n141">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="179.73008481912365" width="90.80478087649408" x="8705.925604334225" y="262.0578115958866"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="180.4140625" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="87.361328125" x="1.7217263757465844" xml:space="preserve" y="-0.34198884043814815">Since the
Roman identity
was largely
held together
because of the
Roman Empire,
should Roman
be split based
regions like
Italian is? Only
under certain
circumstances?<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n6::n142">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="374.39988895548333" width="201.9485794764414" x="8653.050096818602" y="-781.8322588919224"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="371.529296875" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="190.1171875" x="5.91569598822025" xml:space="preserve" y="1.4352960402417239">Outside of Italy, Roman would
likely be replaced by the hybrid
cultures shown to the right (or a
new dynamic hybrid culture for
regions it didn't historically
expand to). Within Italy, Roman
would likely end up remaining,
but, if Rome loses control of
Italy, and the people there
slowly stop seeing themselves as
Roman as new states appear, then
the new regional cultures that are
in EU4/5 need to appear over time.

We could maybe have creation
names to allow these regional
cultures to appear naturally even
if Rome still exists, but should
maybe also have something else
like events that trigger when Rome
loses control of parts of Italy for a
certain amount of time to have any
Roman counties/characters in the
relevent regions begin transitioning
to the historical regional culture.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n6::n143">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="134.90383509350866" width="158.44824016970506" x="10964.179348984551" y="-758.0751892719442"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="136.310546875" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="158.08984375" x="0.1791982098529843" xml:space="preserve" y="-0.7033558907456836">Instead of having a
dedicated Sardino-Roman
culture, could maybe also
just have Sardinia convert
as Roman, and have
Corsican/Sardinian appear
naturally along with the
other regional Italian cultures
if Rome loses control of Italy.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
