        <node id="n6::n169">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="110.95990452117252" width="171.3538616843125" x="7767.5893098657125" y="-473.8538890883187"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="106.908203125" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="173.4296875" x="-1.0379129078437472" xml:space="preserve" y="2.0258506980862308">CK3 seems to use Cisalpine as
a stand-in for the Gallo-Italic
cultures/languages (except for
Lombard, which oddly exists in
South Italy, where it would have
had less of an influence than in
the North).
<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n6::n170">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="179.08141286149822" width="171.3538616843125" x="8102.936239856537" y="-473.8538890883186"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="180.4140625" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="174.783203125" x="-1.7146707203437472" xml:space="preserve" y="-0.6663248192509172">CK3 seems to use Italian as
a stand-in for the Central Italian
cultures/languages. If we went
along this way of simplifying the
cultures, Italian would likely also
be used to represent the
South Italian cultures/languages
as well, at least compared to
Lombard, which they use in the
867 start, until it's replaced by
Sicilian, which is also an
oversimplification.
<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n6::n171">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="92.23837672095564" width="291.79532561178985" x="7852.995554857193" y="-689.6430967193919"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="92.20703125" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="288.1328125" x="1.8312565558944698" xml:space="preserve" y="0.015672735477778588">CK3 simplifies the Italian cultures by doing things like
using Cisalpine for Gallo-Italic, Italian for Central (and
South?) Italian, and possibly Lombard-&gt;Sicilian for
South Italian. We could go along with these cultures,
or just jump straight into separating them into their
regional cultures, like how'd they appear in EU5.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
