        <node id="n9::n49">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:GenericNode configuration="com.yworks.flowchart.terminator">
              <y:Geometry height="40.0" width="80.0" x="6639.808028308562" y="-651.3813689512795"/>
              <y:Fill color="#B7C9E3" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" type="dashed" width="5.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="18.701171875" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#FF0000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="60.712890625" x="9.6435546875" xml:space="preserve" y="10.6494140625">Aquitanian<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
            </y:GenericNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n9::n50">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="384.29791532845337" width="129.18536252642957" x="6615.215347045348" y="-611.3813689512795"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="386.23046875" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="130.076171875" x="-0.4454046742848732" xml:space="preserve" y="-0.9662767107732861">TFE has Aquitanian
which gets used for
culture mappings in
most places when
using it, but the culture
doesn't seem to really
get used in TFE itself.

While the Vascones
and Aquitanians were
likely closely related,
it is expected that the
Vascones are the
Basque's main
ancestors since they
ended up resisting
Romanization, and kept
their language, but it'd
probably be fine to
map both to Basque
given how closely
related they were. It
just needs to be
determined whether we
will prefer Basque or
Aquitanian for TFE.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
