              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="165.712890625" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="190.099609375" x="1.53949400161855" xml:space="preserve" y="-0.4370185848051733">Andalusi Arabic and the Spanish
Romance languages did influence
each other a little, so not sure if
Andalusian should be a hybrid of
Maghrebi with a Romance Spanish
culture, or just Maghrebi diverging
in Iberia. That would likely depend
on whether we want the existance
of the Andalusians to depend on
whether Rome properly converted
