              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="195.115234375" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="178.41015625" x="0.2369892120905206" xml:space="preserve" y="0.15385370627487305">The Britano-Romans likely didn't
adopt Latin as much as other
peoples throughout the Roman
Empire, and as such, the
Britano-Romans are also often
considered "ancestors" to the
other divergent Brythonic here.
Not sure if we should allow
Britano-Roman to diverge into
them as well at any time, or only
if it seems like (in game), Rome
didn't control Britain long enough
to properly spread Latin there.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
