        <node id="n11::n133">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:GenericNode configuration="com.yworks.flowchart.terminator">
              <y:Geometry height="40.0" width="80.0" x="8173.728478306381" y="-89.04940972670482"/>
              <y:Fill color="#B7C9E3" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="18.701171875" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#008000" underlinedText="true" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="42.021484375" x="18.9892578125" xml:space="preserve" y="10.6494140625">Arpitan<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
            </y:GenericNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n11::n134">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="179.57653833570294" width="257.6273442171903" x="8084.914806197786" y="11.58794120399051"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="180.4140625" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="250.796875" x="3.415234608594801" xml:space="preserve" y="-0.4187620821485325">It seems like Arpitan could be considered
a separate language from d'oil and d'oc, so
it's hard to say what should be done about
it. EU5 seems to classify it as French, but
not sure how accurate that is.

It should probably have it's own culture in
CK3, but I'm not sure exactly how it should be
created. It seems like it's an entirely separate
branch from French and Occitan, so we could
probably just have Gallo-Roman in the region
diverge into Arpitan instead of Occitan/French.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n11::n135">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:ShapeNode>
              <y:Geometry height="83.21940047298801" width="222.2265370821642" x="8253.72847830638" y="-132.26881019969295"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFCC00" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="77.505859375" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="222.12109375" x="0.05272166608119733" xml:space="preserve" y="2.8567705489940067">There are two creation names for this,
one depends on you diverging with a
Frankish Heritage in the region, the other
depends on you hybridizing a Frankish
and Latin Heritage cultures in the region.<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
              <y:Shape type="rectangle"/>
            </y:ShapeNode>
          </data>
        </node>
        <node id="n11::n136">
          <data key="d6">
            <y:GenericNode configuration="com.yworks.flowchart.terminator">
